"""Distinct design decisions for legacy comparison routes; no invented provider ratings."""
# slug, title, focus, practical explanation, hypothetical worked decision, acceptance check, related guide
DATA=[
('ai-design-tools','AI design tools for STR owners: concept to usable plan','Validate the gap between a rendered idea and a buildable room.','An AI image can help explore a palette or furniture arrangement, but a convincing image does not establish dimensions, load capacity, safe installation, product availability or a complete purchase list. Keep the original room photographs and measured plan beside every concept. Assign a person to reconcile the image with the property before sourcing.','A generated living room shows two sofas and a work desk. The measured plan reveals that the second sofa blocks the path from the kitchen. Retain the color direction, replace the furniture arrangement, and specify a smaller desk with accessible power and a chair that can be used without moving other furniture.','Produce a product schedule with actual dimensions and a measured route through the furnished room. Reject selections that cannot be traced to an available product or an approved custom specification.','/learn/studio-rental-zoning-without-extra-furniture/'),
('facebook-marketplace-furnishing','Facebook Marketplace furnishing for an Airbnb','Evaluate condition and replacement risk before judging the bargain.','Secondhand sourcing requires an item-by-item inspection rather than an assumption that a photographed piece will arrive in guest-ready condition. Check dimensions, stability, odor, visible damage, missing parts and the manufacturer’s instructions where available. Account for collection, transport, cleaning and disposal of an unsuitable item. Do not treat a seller description as proof of commercial suitability.','An owner finds six dining chairs from different sellers. The purchase looks inexpensive, but inconsistent seat heights and two loose joints make the group unsuitable for one table. Inspect a complete seating arrangement before buying and price a coordinated replacement option alongside the used set.','Record condition photographs, dimensions, transport cost and a realistic replacement route. For safety-sensitive products, verify identity and recalls using the official product information before use.','/resources/guides/keep-repair-replace-audit/'),
('general-contractor-furnishing','General contractor or STR designer: divide the scope','Separate building work from guest-ready furnishing.','A contractor and a designer can contribute to the same property without providing the same deliverables. Building work may involve trades, installation conditions and permits, while furnishing adds layout, product selection, delivery, household inventory and guest-use checks. Define the boundary at each interface: a finished outlet does not mean a lamp has been selected, and a painted wall does not mean artwork is installed.','A bathroom refresh is nearly complete when the owner realizes that towel storage and mirror lighting were never in the furnishing list. Review the construction scope against the guest routine before finalizing finishes, then allocate accessories, mounting, cleaning and testing to named roles.','Create an interface list showing which party supplies, installs, checks and accepts each item. Confirm required qualifications and local requirements for the actual building work with appropriate professionals.','/learn/bathroom-refresh-design-brief/'),
('hotel-design-firm','Hotel design firm or STR studio: match the brief','Translate hospitality experience to a whole-home guest routine.','Hotel-style specifications can be valuable, but a rental home may combine cooking, laundry, remote work, outdoor activities and group travel within one booking. Ask how the proposed service addresses those routines and who handles the small operating items that a hotel might supply centrally. Compare the actual assignment rather than assuming either studio category is automatically more durable.','An eight-person rental receives a hotel-inspired bedroom concept, but the living room seats four and the kitchen has one small meal-preparation surface. Extend the brief to shared-room capacity and cooking workflow before approving the bedrooms as the project’s main investment.','Ask for a capacity matrix spanning beds, dining, lounge seating, tableware and outdoor use. Evaluate cleaning access and replacement logistics alongside the visual concept.','/resources/guides/guest-capacity-furnishing-matrix/'),
('pinterest-diy','Pinterest DIY Airbnb design: turn inspiration into a plan','Use inspiration images as references, then specify your actual rooms.','An inspiration board communicates atmosphere but usually mixes different room sizes, light conditions and product scales. Annotate each saved image with the quality you want: contrast, texture, storage, lighting or a focal point. A clear annotation helps you avoid trying to copy an entire room that cannot fit your property. Build the layout before purchasing decor.','A coastal board contains pale upholstery, large pendants and open shelving. The actual rental has a narrow kitchen and frequent family stays. Keep the palette, choose washable finishes and enclosed storage, and test pendant placement against the real ceiling and dining layout.','Every inspiration choice should lead to a measurable requirement, a specified product or a documented material test. Remove images that add conflicting directions without solving a guest need.','/blog/tropical-color-palette-guide.html'),
('professional-stager','Professional staging or STR design: guest use matters','Distinguish a photograph-ready space from an operating rental.','Staging may be scoped around a presentation date, while a rental design assignment must also consider repeated guest use, cleaning, storage and ownership of the furnishings. Either professional can help if those requirements are included. Ask whether pieces are purchased or temporarily supplied, how long they remain and who replaces them after the initial installation.','A staged lounge photographs well, but a small decorative coffee table is unstable during board games and the furniture must be returned after a short hire period. Before relaunch, specify a suitable owned table and document the removal date of temporary pieces.','Run a seated-use and reset walkthrough with the actual cleaner. Confirm ownership, condition responsibilities and replacement arrangements before publishing listing photographs.','/blog/airbnb-photography-guide.html'),
('real-estate-agent-staging','Real estate staging for a rental: adapt the objective','Ask whether the work prepares a sale or a guest stay.','A sales presentation is designed to help a prospective buyer understand a home. A rental setup must support sleeping, cooking, working, unpacking and turnover after the photographs are taken. If an agent offers staging support, request a separate rental-ready inventory and distinguish marketing assistance from ongoing operating responsibilities.','A property remains on the rental market while the owner considers a future sale. Use durable owned essentials for guests and decide which decorative items are temporary. Photograph the version guests will actually receive, and record the changeover plan if the home is later staged for sale.','Check that every advertised bed, seat, desk and appliance remains available for the booked stay. Document who handles changes between guest bookings and sales showings.','/learn/reference/identity/'),
('virtual-interior-designer','Virtual interior design for Airbnb: a complete handoff','Make local execution part of the design budget.','Remote design can work when property information is reliable and local responsibilities are assigned. Provide dimensioned plans, ceiling heights, window details, outlet locations, photographs and retained-furniture measurements. Decide who resolves discrepancies, approves substitutes and verifies installed results. A sourcing list is one deliverable; receiving and assembly are separate tasks unless contracted.','An owner receives a complete bedroom concept but measures only wall-to-wall width. The bed fits the room while its headboard cannot pass the stair turn. Add packaging dimensions, the delivery path and access restrictions to the approval process before ordering.','A usable handoff names each item, quantity, dimension, finish, placement, care instruction and approved alternative. Assign a local measurement verifier and final walkthrough lead.','/compare/full-service-vs-design-only/'),
('mybnbdesign-vs-amazon-furnishing.html','Amazon furnishing or a design service for your STR','Compare a product marketplace with a complete project scope.','A marketplace gives access to individual products; it does not automatically provide a coordinated room plan or one accountable installation team. Verify the seller, exact variant, instructions, return conditions and delivery method for each purchase. Use a single inventory to coordinate products from different sellers and avoid counting a design-service fee as though it were a furniture price.','A bedroom order includes a bed, mattress and bedside tables from separate listings. One listing changes dimensions between sizes and another arrives after the planned photo date. Record exact variants and acceptance dates, then approve substitutes against the complete bedroom layout.','Keep order identifiers, product specifications, condition photos and return deadlines together. Confirm who assembles, removes packaging and checks the final room.','/resources/guides/scope-before-shopping/'),
('mybnbdesign-vs-ikea-airbnb.html','IKEA furnishing for Airbnb: plan assembly and replacement','Budget the complete installed inventory.','A coordinated retail range can simplify visual selection, but delivery, carrying, assembly, anchoring, hardware and replacement work still need owners. Confirm the instructions for the actual item and the room’s intended use. Compare a self-managed shopping plan with a service proposal only after adding the labor and logistics needed to reach the same finished condition.','A group rental uses several matching dressers. The owner budgets the products but no assembly window or appropriate installation support. Plan one room first, verify the finished dimensions and instructions, and use that experience to estimate the remaining workload.','Track quantity, variant, spare hardware information, care guidance and replacement availability. Follow manufacturer instructions and obtain qualified installation where required.','/learn/reference/storage/'),
('mybnbdesign-vs-pottery-barn-str.html','Pottery Barn furnishing for STRs: specify use and care','Choose by operating requirements rather than brand impression.','A retail brand can offer a useful aesthetic direction, but suitability must be established for the particular material, construction and intended use. Compare dimensions, upholstery care, finish requirements, lead times and replacement options. Ask the seller about the product’s applicable warranty terms for your intended rental use rather than assuming a residential warranty covers every setting.','An owner selects a pale sofa for a pet-friendly rental. Before ordering, request the actual care information and inspect a material sample under the property’s light. Compare maintenance effort and replacement cushion availability with a darker or differently textured alternative.','Keep the exact fabric or finish designation with the purchase record. Give cleaners the applicable care instructions and test permitted cleaning methods on a sample first.','/resources/damage-resistant-materials/'),
('mybnbdesign-vs-target-budget-design.html','Target budget furnishing for Airbnb: spend by priority','Build a room budget around essential functions first.','A budget furnishing project needs a clear boundary between essential guest functions and optional styling. List sleeping, seating, lighting, storage and dining requirements before accessories. Retail sourcing can support that plan, but selecting attractive items from a store does not determine whether they fit together, remain available or withstand your maintenance routine.','An owner has a fixed living-room budget and plans a large decor order before selecting seating. Reverse the sequence: reserve funds for adequate usable seats, task lighting and a stable surface, then choose a limited set of accessories with the remaining amount.','Record the quantity and landed cost of each essential item, including tax and setup. Recheck the total whenever a product or delivery arrangement changes.','/blog/how-to-decorate-airbnb-on-a-budget/'),
('blueground-design','Blueground or independent STR design: different engagements','Compare an operating or leasing relationship with a design contract.','Blueground’s U.S. property-owner page describes furnished housing and leasing arrangements. That is not evidence that every owner can purchase a standalone design package. Confirm the relationship offered for your property, including lease structure, furniture ownership, maintenance and exit conditions, before comparing it with a separately contracted designer.','A multifamily owner wants to furnish units while retaining control of bookings. First decide whether the objective is a design deliverable or a furnished-housing operating agreement. Compare proposed cash obligations and operational responsibilities only after that decision.','Request the actual agreement and inventory ownership schedule. Verify what remains with the property when the relationship ends.','/learn/portfolio-furnishing-standard-with-local-variation/'),
('kasa-living-design','Kasa or STR design services: clarify the partnership','Separate hospitality operations from a design-only assignment.','Kasa’s property-partner material describes operating hospitality properties with real-estate partners. An attractive Kasa interior does not establish a retail design package for an individual host. Ask about property eligibility and the complete partnership arrangement, then compare a design firm only if it is solving the same problem.','A boutique-property owner seeks both a guest concept and operating support. Develop two briefs: one for physical design and furnishing and another for management and guest operations. Some proposals may combine them, but the costs and responsibilities should remain visible.','Identify who approves furnishing standards, owns the goods, maintains them and funds replacements. Confirm how design decisions interact with operating requirements.','/learn/portfolio-furnishing-standard-with-local-variation/'),
('frontdesk-design','Frontdesk design references: verify the current offer','Do not infer a purchasable design service from accommodation branding.','The legacy comparison did not establish a current, verified standalone design offer for the named service. Before using accommodation photographs as evidence of a design contract, identify the responsible company and obtain current written terms. Treat an inspiring room as a reference until its product specifications and implementation model are known.','An owner finds an older article about a furnished-apartment operator and assumes its interiors can be purchased as a package. Ask for a current official proposal first. If no such service is available, use the photographs only to articulate the desired guest experience to a verified design team.','Require current business identity, address eligibility, deliverables and an accountable contact. Do not send a deposit based only on an old brand mention.','/resources/guides/scope-before-shopping/'),
('sonder-interior-design','Sonder interior-design references: verify availability','Separate a hospitality design reference from an available service.','This page does not establish a current standalone Sonder design service or its availability. The previous comparison treated a hospitality brand as an interchangeable design contractor without evidence. Owners can still learn from a room’s organization, but the design should be translated into their own measured requirements and a verified provider proposal.','A host likes the visual consistency of a furnished-hospitality room. Write down the useful principles—clear circulation, limited finishes and easy-to-find lighting—then test those principles in the actual rental instead of assuming the original operator can furnish it.','Ask any provider for a dated service description, legal entity, delivery terms and project contacts before comparing fees or making a commitment.','/learn/reference/identity/'),
('vacasa-design-services','Vacasa design services: confirm current owner eligibility','Check management requirements before treating design as standalone.','Vacasa has published an interior-design program for homes in its managed portfolio. The cited program announcement is historical and does not establish today’s packages, pricing or eligibility. Request current written terms for the property and separate the design assignment from any required management relationship.','A homeowner wants a refresh while continuing with a local manager. Determine whether the proposed design service is available under that arrangement before comparing its fee with an independent designer. Include any ongoing operating commitment in the decision.','Record current eligibility, selected package, purchasing and installation scope, management terms and the end-of-project handoff.','/compare/full-service-vs-design-only/'),
('airbnb-design-co','Airbnb design company proposal: verify the provider','Resolve the exact business behind a broad design-company name.','A broad phrase such as Airbnb Design Co can point to more than one business or a category of service. The legacy page did not establish a unique official provider. Do not transfer reviews, prices or portfolio photographs from a similarly named studio. Begin with the legal entity, official domain and a directly confirmed proposal.','An owner has a branded mood board but an invoice bearing a different entity. Ask how those names relate and confirm the agreement through an official contact. Only then evaluate the room plan and payment milestones.','Keep the official contact, business identity, signed scope and sample deliverable together. Match any referenced project to the team actually proposing the work.','/best-airbnb-design-companies/'),
('beyond-stay-design','Beyond Stay Design: evaluate a rental design brief','Verify identity, then test the guest brief.','The previous page lacked sufficient official evidence for the specific provider it described. Current pricing, coverage and outcomes are not established here. An owner can still evaluate the proposed design brief by checking how it identifies the target guest, the property’s constraints and the routines the layout must support.','A proposed brief says the rental suits everyone. Rewrite it around a concrete stay, such as two couples sharing meals and working occasionally. Test whether the actual seating, privacy, dining and storage choices support that stay before approving the style direction.','Request a dated brief with intended guests, retained items, room priorities, exclusions and the owner’s approval process.','/learn/large-group-activity-zoning/'),
('chic-retreats-design','Chic Retreats Design: assess a proposed style direction','Translate a style label into materials and a measured layout.','The legacy page did not verify a specific provider behind this name. No comparative rating is assigned. If a proposal uses retreat or boutique styling, ask how its material palette, lighting and furniture scale respond to your property rather than relying on a style label to establish suitability.','A retreat concept uses dark walls, low lighting and several fragile accessories. Test one material and lighting combination in the real room, then evaluate whether guests can read, unpack and clean the space without losing the intended mood.','Require material samples, actual product dimensions and a guest-use walkthrough before approving the final specification.','/blog/tropical-color-palette-guide.html'),
('inhabit-designer','Inhabit Designer: check the room-planning deliverables','Verify the provider and the accuracy of the space plan.','The named comparison did not contain enough official evidence to establish a current provider offering. The useful decision is whether the proposed room plan is based on reliable measurements and shows the way guests move through the furnished space. Ask for the dimension source and the revision process before ordering.','A plan places a king bed between two windows using an approximate room width. Measure the trim, outlets, door swing and headboard before approving the bed. A revised layout may preserve the guest capacity while preventing a costly return.','Ask who verifies dimensions, how errors are corrected and whether delivery-path checks are included. Keep the approved plan version with every purchase order.','/learn/reference/sleep/'),
('rental-design-lab','Rental Design Lab: review the implementation handoff','Distinguish a general name from a verified studio and service.','Rental Design Lab and STR Design Lab should not be assumed to be the same business. This page does not verify a separate provider under the former name. For any remote design offer, examine how the final handoff converts concepts into product selections, quantities and room-by-room instructions.','A local installer receives a shopping spreadsheet with no item placement or mounting information. Ask the designer for a room plan, exact product variants and instructions for unresolved interfaces before the installer starts.','Require a sample complete handoff, an approved substitution process and a named contact for implementation questions.','/compare/virtual-interior-designer/'),
('str-design-studio','STR design studio: choose a measurable service scope','Use a generic studio label as the beginning of a scope discussion.','STR design studio describes a category as well as possible business names. The legacy page did not establish one specific provider. Evaluate the proposed service by its deliverables: guest strategy, measured layouts, furnishings, procurement, installation and operating handoff. Mark each as included, excluded or awaiting confirmation.','An owner receives a single fee for a studio package. Break it into the decisions and tasks required for the property, then identify who handles delivery damage, missing products, final cleaning and photography readiness.','A complete scope identifies the responsible party, completion evidence and acceptance date for every major task. Resolve unknowns before comparing prices.','/top-str-design-services/'),
('turnkey-vr-design','Turnkey vacation-rental design: define guest-ready','Test a turnkey promise against the last unfinished tasks.','The old comparison did not establish a specific verified provider called Turnkey VR Design. Turnkey is useful only when the contract defines the finished condition. Furniture assembly, safe installation, household stocking, electronics setup, cleaning and photo staging may belong to different people unless deliberately coordinated.','A home is described as turnkey after furniture is assembled, but the bedrooms lack linens and the Wi-Fi has not been tested. Write an acceptance checklist that follows an actual guest arrival, evening, meal and checkout rather than counting delivered boxes.','Confirm who signs off on each room, closes the punch list and supplies the final product and care records.','/learn/furnishing-project-critical-path/')]
APPROACHES={r[0]:dict(zip(['key','title','focus','explanation','scenario','test','related'],r)) for r in DATA}
